{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Equiv","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TemperleyLiebTower"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.traceRadical_eq_zero_of_algEquiv_pi_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.traceRadical_eq_zero_of_algEquiv_pi_matrix","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceRadicalNondegenerate.lean#L202-L223","doc":"**The shape the Temperley–Lieb application needs.**\n\nIf `A` decomposes as a finite product of matrix algebras and `τ` is the weighted\nblock trace pulled back along that decomposition, then `τ` has **zero radical**\nprovided no weight vanishes.\n\nApplied to `TL_n(δ)`: the two inputs are (i) the Wedderburn decomposition, still\nopen, and (ii) `y_λ ≠ 0`, which `QOU.QBeta.TemperleyLiebTower.yw_pos` already\nsupplies for `1 < q`. So this reduces the `⊇` half of\n`⟨relators⟩ = traceRadical tr_M` to the decomposition alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.traceRadical_comp_algEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.traceRadical_comp_algEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceRadicalNondegenerate.lean#L175-L190","doc":"**The trace radical transports along an algebra isomorphism.**\n\nOnly surjectivity and multiplicativity are used, so this holds for any\n`τ : B → K` whatever — no trace axioms needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.weightedBlockTrace_traceRadical_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.weightedBlockTrace_traceRadical_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceRadicalNondegenerate.lean#L137-L164","doc":"**The nonzero-weight hypothesis cannot be dropped.**\n\nIf `y j = 0` and the `j`-th block is not the zero algebra, then that whole block\nlies in the radical, so the radical is strictly bigger than `{0}`. The witness is\nthe identity of the `j`-th block, sitting at `j` and zero elsewhere.\n\nStated so that `weightedBlockTrace_traceRadical_eq_zero`'s hypothesis is visibly\nload-bearing rather than decorative: with it the radical vanishes, without it —\nat any single index — it does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.weightedBlockTrace_traceRadical_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.weightedBlockTrace_traceRadical_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceRadicalNondegenerate.lean#L107-L135","doc":"**The radical of a weighted block trace is zero exactly when no weight\nvanishes — the `←` direction.**\n\nIf some `y_j = 0` the `j`-th block is invisible to `τ` and lies in the radical;\nwith every weight nonzero, testing against `Pi.single j x` isolates one block and\n`matrix_eq_zero_of_forall_trace_mul` finishes it.\n\nThe weights are where the content is: this is the formal statement of \"the trace\nsees every block\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.weightedBlockTrace_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.weightedBlockTrace_zero","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceRadicalNondegenerate.lean#L103-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.weightedBlockTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.weightedBlockTrace","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceRadicalNondegenerate.lean#L94-L100","doc":"**The weighted block trace** `τ(a) = Σ_i y_i · tr(a_i)` on a finite product\nof matrix algebras.\n\nThis is the shape of every Markov trace in this corpus: `tr_M = Σ_λ y_λ χ_λ`,\nwith the `y_λ` the Wedderburn weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.matrix_eq_zero_of_forall_trace_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.matrix_eq_zero_of_forall_trace_mul","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceRadicalNondegenerate.lean#L78-L82","doc":"The form of the above actually used below: pairing to zero against every\nmatrix forces vanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.matrix_traceRadical_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceRadicalNondegenerate.matrix_traceRadical_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceRadicalNondegenerate.lean#L59-L75","doc":"**The matrix trace form has zero radical.**\n\nA restatement of `Matrix.ext_iff_trace_mul_right` in the `traceRadical`\nvocabulary this corpus uses. Kept because the translation is where the two\nlibraries meet, not because the content is new. ","signatureChunk":0}]}